Janis Papanagnou wrote:
> James wrote:
> 
>> I just got an interesting sequence of messages, which suggests a
>> bug.  I just found the vibrating square.  I'm carrying the
>> candelabra and the bell, and I've got the candles in my blessed
>> BoH.  I take them out, and become burdened.  I apply them to the
>> candelabra, and become unburdened.  Are the candles really
>> supposed to weigh less when attached to the candelabra?
> 
> Once attached they are implemented just as a counter, not as objects
> with weight. It is a known issue, and, I think, considered not worth
> a fix.

Ok. But the fix was so easy that I coded it anyway:

--- CUT HERE!---
diff -bruNX ignore.txt ..\official/src/mkobj.c ./src/mkobj.c
--- ..\official/src/mkobj.c	Fri Aug 25 18:46:24 2006
+++ ./src/mkobj.c	Mon Sep 24 13:36:18 2007
@@ -852,6 +852,8 @@
  		return (int)((obj->quan + 50L) / 100L);
  	else if (obj->otyp == HEAVY_IRON_BALL && obj->owt != 0)
  		return((int)(obj->owt));	/* kludge for "very" heavy iron ball */
+	else if (obj->otyp == CANDELABRUM_OF_INVOCATION)
+		return(wt + 2*(int)obj->spe);
  	return(wt ? wt*(int)obj->quan : ((int)obj->quan + 1)>>1);
  }
